{
  "source": "course-assets/curiosity/curiosity.mp4",
  "duration": 183.3173125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.12,
      "text": "Imagine you are the captain of your school's basketball team."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.82,
      "end": 6.22,
      "text": "You have a play that has worked beautifully all season."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.02,
      "end": 10.24,
      "text": "But suddenly, another team figures out how to shut it down."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.88,
      "end": 13.62,
      "text": "Before you find a better play, you need to be curious."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.3,
      "end": 16.0,
      "text": "You have to diagnose the failure."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.7,
      "end": 18.84,
      "text": "What exactly is the opponent doing differently?"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.44,
      "end": 20.44,
      "text": "Where is the new opening?"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.86,
      "end": 22.9,
      "text": "What could you learn by watching that play again?"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.76,
      "end": 27.92,
      "text": "Taking an active interest, asking questions, and exploring possibilities"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.92,
      "end": 30.2,
      "text": "reaches far beyond the basketball court."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.76,
      "end": 32.98,
      "text": "It helps you keep learning throughout your entire life."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.58,
      "end": 34.88,
      "text": "There's always more to discover."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.82,
      "end": 38.84,
      "text": "In this first panel, curiosity acts as your armor."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.64,
      "end": 41.9,
      "text": "Influencers, advertisers, and algorithms"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.9,
      "end": 44.38,
      "text": "are constantly trying to shape what you think."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.0,
      "end": 46.66,
      "text": "When you encounter persuasive media,"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.96,
      "end": 48.38,
      "text": "ask defensive questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.86,
      "end": 50.18,
      "text": "Who wants me to believe this?"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.56,
      "end": 51.44,
      "text": "What is the evidence?"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.86,
      "end": 54.06,
      "text": "And what crucial information is missing?"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.06,
      "end": 59.36,
      "text": "Over on the right, curiosity kills boredom. A good question makes ordinary"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.36,
      "end": 64.56,
      "text": "things interesting. Ask how a specific system works, why people choose to do it"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.56,
      "end": 68.78,
      "text": "that particular way, and consider what could be done differently. Curiosity"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.78,
      "end": 73.06,
      "text": "helps you grow by changing how you handle feedback. You will receive"
    },
    {
      "start": 73.06,
      "end": 77.08,
      "text": "critical feedback throughout your life. Instead of shutting down, ask active"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.08,
      "end": 82.32,
      "text": "questions. Find out exactly what worked, pinpoint what could improve, and ask for"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.32,
      "end": 87.62,
      "text": "specific example so you can extract actionable steps. Finally, as this last"
    },
    {
      "start": 87.62,
      "end": 92.86,
      "text": "panel explains, you can learn as you live. It is perfectly acceptable if you"
    },
    {
      "start": 92.86,
      "end": 97.24,
      "text": "do not have your life figured out today. The key is to stay engaged, try"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.24,
      "end": 101.3,
      "text": "new things, meet new people, and pay close attention to what genuinely"
    },
    {
      "start": 101.3,
      "end": 105.66,
      "text": "captures your interest. Let the things you discover organically map out your"
    },
    {
      "start": 105.66,
      "end": 110.86,
      "text": "next best step. Today, the rapid evolution of artificial intelligence is"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.86,
      "end": 111.94,
      "text": "the ultimate unknown."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.7,
      "end": 114.74,
      "text": "New models, tools, and workflows"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.74,
      "end": 116.28,
      "text": "keep appearing almost daily."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.98,
      "end": 119.38,
      "text": "You do not need to chase every single new feature."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.84,
      "end": 121.22,
      "text": "You only need to stay curious"
    },
    {
      "start": 121.22,
      "end": 123.72,
      "text": "about the changes that could actually matter to you."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.32,
      "end": 127.24,
      "text": "Use this four-part framework to stay AI curious."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.94,
      "end": 130.36,
      "text": "The first habit is to use AI regularly,"
    },
    {
      "start": 130.82,
      "end": 133.1,
      "text": "especially outside of your required schoolwork."
    },
    {
      "start": 133.56,
      "end": 136.28,
      "text": "This baseline familiarity makes it much easier"
    },
    {
      "start": 136.28,
      "end": 139.06,
      "text": "to notice when an interface suddenly gains new abilities."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.06,
      "end": 145.24,
      "text": "Next, you should check what changed. Look out for update notices, new buttons, or model names."
    },
    {
      "start": 145.92,
      "end": 150.32,
      "text": "Constant monitoring isn't necessary. Checking occasionally gives you the information you need."
    },
    {
      "start": 151.0,
      "end": 154.38,
      "text": "To avoid feeling overwhelmed, follow one reliable source."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.92,
      "end": 159.04,
      "text": "Pick a single, trustworthy newsletter, educator, or official product page."
    },
    {
      "start": 159.66,
      "end": 164.62,
      "text": "Calling your inputs down to one curated feed provides enough information to stay informed."
    },
    {
      "start": 164.62,
      "end": 170.88,
      "text": "Finally, compare with others. Ask your friends, teachers, or club members what they have tried recently."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.6,
      "end": 174.66,
      "text": "Different people naturally stumble upon different tools and features."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.14,
      "end": 176.54,
      "text": "Curiosity keeps you growing."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.28,
      "end": 179.9,
      "text": "Keep asking questions. Keep learning as you live."
    }
  ],
